            <ArticleTitle>Dissection of the aorta and coronary arteries associated with acute cocaine intoxication.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1239-41</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acute myocardial ischemia, cardiac arrhythmias, and conduction disturbances are the most common cardiovascular complications of cocaine and its alkaloidal freebase &quot;crack.&quot; Cocaine abuse-related acute aortic dissection has been reported only rarely: three cases in the last 5 years. Described herein, to our knowledge, is the first case of cocaine intoxication-associated acute aortic dissection that also involved the coronary arteries, causing sudden death.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
